---
import './design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from './SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from './SketchArrow.astro';
---
<figure id="unique-write-timeline" class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface unique-timeline" aria-labelledby="unique-write-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Concurrent writes</span>
  <h3 id="unique-write-title">Two requests try to claim CUP-GREEN</h3>
  <p>Two requests want to create a product with SKU <code>CUP-GREEN</code>. The SKU identifies a catalogue product and must be unique. Neither request has inserted a row when the checks run.</p>
  <div class="time-direction"><span class="direction-label"><SketchArrow direction="down" /> Time runs down</span><span>With <code>UNIQUE (sku)</code></span></div>
  <SketchSheet>
  <table>
    <caption class="visually-hidden">A concurrent insert sequence with a PostgreSQL unique constraint</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request A · product P11</th><th scope="col">Request B · product P12</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="event"><strong>Check CUP-GREEN</strong><span>No row found.</span></td><td class="event"><strong>Check CUP-GREEN</strong><span>No row found.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td class="event"><strong>Insert P11</strong><span>SKU: CUP-GREEN.<br />Still uncommitted.</span></td><td class="waiting" rowspan="2"><strong>Try to insert P12</strong><span>Same SKU: CUP-GREEN.</span><strong class="wait-label">Wait for A</strong><span>Continues until A commits or rolls back.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td class="event finish"><strong>Commit</strong><span>P11 is stored.<br />B’s wait ends here.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td class="ended">A’s transaction ended.</td><td class="event finish"><strong>Uniqueness error</strong><span>A committed the SKU.<br />B’s insert is rejected.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </SketchSheet>
  <div class="unique-final"><strong>Stored result</strong><span><code>P11 · CUP-GREEN</code> only</span></div>
  <figcaption>The checks describe what each request saw; they reserve nothing. Here an ordinary, immediate PostgreSQL UNIQUE constraint decides the conflicting writes. If A rolled back, B could proceed. Without database enforcement or another coordination mechanism, both checks could be followed by committed duplicates. This sequence shows order, not elapsed time.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .time-direction { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.5rem; margin:.8rem 0; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.8125rem; }
  .direction-label { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.45rem; }
  .direction-label :global(svg) { height:2.5rem; width:1.6rem; }
  table { table-layout:fixed; }
  .design-aid td { position:relative; padding:.8rem .5rem .9rem 1.2rem; border:0; }
  .design-aid th { padding-left:1.2rem; }
  td strong,td span { display:block; }
  td span { margin-top:.25rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .event::before { content:''; position:absolute; left:.35rem; top:0; bottom:0; border-left:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .event::after { content:''; position:absolute; left:.18rem; bottom:.1rem; width:.4rem; height:.4rem; border-right:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); transform:rotate(45deg); }
  .waiting::before { content:''; position:absolute; left:.16rem; top:0; bottom:0; width:.4rem; border-left:1px solid var(--gold); border-right:1px solid var(--gold); background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,transparent 0 4px,color-mix(in srgb,var(--gold) 55%,transparent) 4px 5px); }
  .waiting strong { color:var(--gold); }
  .waiting .wait-label { margin-top:1rem; }
  .finish::after { height:0; width:.5rem; left:.1rem; border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); transform:none; }
  .ended { color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .unique-final { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.6rem 1.4rem; align-items:baseline; border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:.75rem .5rem; margin-top:.6rem; background:linear-gradient(178deg,transparent 5%,var(--paper-match) 8% 92%,transparent 95%); }
  @media(max-width:420px) { .design-aid td,.design-aid th { padding-right:.25rem; padding-left:.9rem; } }
</style>
